% Twinkle Twinkle Little Star — ABC notation test fixture.
%
% Public-domain melody: traditional, popularised via Mozart's K. 265
% variations and the English lyric by Jane Taylor (1806). All
% comfortably out of copyright everywhere TWANGA ships.
%
% Encoded as ABC because ABC is the dominant text-based notation
% format in folk / traditional music circles (banjo, mandolin,
% fiddle, ukulele — exactly TWANGA's niche), so having a real ABC
% fixture next to the .musicxml / .alphatex equivalents lets the
% importer integration tests assert the same melody parses
% consistently across every supported text format.
%
% Fixture under MIT OR Apache-2.0, matching the rest of the TWANGA
% repo.

X:1
T:Twinkle Twinkle Little Star
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=100
K:C
C C G G | A A G2 |
